# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 9 of the Tutorial

[AS7's Examples 12.2 & 12.6 (balanced wye-wye)]

ea0,ag,0,(110∠0°)
eb0,bg,0,(110∠-120°)
ec0,cg,0,(110∠120°)
rat,ag,ad,5-2j
rbt,bg,bd,5-2j
rct,cg,cd,5-2j
ra0,ad,0,10+8j
rb0,bd,0,10+8j
rc0,cd,0,10+8j

analysis: ac
note: Calculate the line currents of the three-wire Y-Y system, and the complex power absorbed at the source and at the load; the values are RMS. The centre of both wyes can be node 0 only because the system is balanced. Complex power at the source is -2086.2 - 834.5j VA, and at the load sra0+srb0+src0 = 1390.8 + 1112.6j VA.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7e1202.png
omega: omega
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: yes
polar: yes
evaluate: sea0+seb0+sec0


[AS7's Practice Problem 12.2 & 12.6 (three impedances a line)]

ea0,ag,0,(120∠30°)
eb0,bg,0,(120∠-90°)
ec0,cg,0,(120∠150°)
rag,ag,as,.4+.3j
rbg,bg,bs,.4+.3j
rcg,cg,cs,.4+.3j
rat,as,ad,.6+.7j
rbt,bs,bd,.6+.7j
rct,cs,cd,.6+.7j
ra0,ad,0,24+19j
rb0,bd,0,24+19j
rc0,cd,0,24+19j

analysis: ac
note: Calculate the line voltages, the line currents, and the complex power at the source and at the load; RMS again. Line voltages depend on where you stand: vag-vbg is 207.8 at 60 deg at the generator, 204.6 at 60.03 at the start of the line, 198.7 at 59.71 at its end. Source complex power -1054 - 842.9j VA.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7pp1202.png
omega: omega
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: yes
polar: yes
evaluate: sea0+seb0+sec0


[AS7's Example 12.10 (unbalanced wye-wye)]

ea,a,0,(120∠0°)
eb,b,0,(120∠-120°)
ec,c,0,(120∠120°)
ra,a,n,5j
rb,b,n,10
rc,c,n,-10j

analysis: ac
note: Find the line currents and the total complex power absorbed by the load and by the source. Unbalanced, so the load's centre needs its own node and its voltage is not zero. Complex power is conserved: sea+seb+sec+sra+srb+src comes to nothing.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7e1210.png
omega: omega
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: yes
polar: yes
evaluate: vn


[AS7's Example 12.9 (unbalanced, with a neutral)]

ea,a,0,(100∠0°)
eb,b,0,(100∠120°)
ec,c,0,(100∠-120°)
sn,0,n
ra,a,n,15
rb,b,n,10+5j
rc,c,n,6-8j

analysis: ac
note: Calculate the line currents and the neutral current — aa(isn) — for the unbalanced Y-load with voltages in the acb sequence. Not RMS this time. The neutral is a short circuit, and it carries a current precisely because the load is unbalanced.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7f1223.png
omega: omega
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes


[AS7's Example 12.3 (balanced wye-delta)]

ea0,a,0,(100∠10°)
eb0,b,0,(100∠-110°)
ec0,c,0,(100∠130°)
rab,a,b,8+4j
rca,c,a,8+4j
rbc,b,c,8+4j

analysis: ac
note: Find the phase currents (irab, irbc, irca) and the line currents (the Evaluate line, -iea0, and its two siblings). The line current is root-three times the phase current and lags it by 30 degrees, which the answers show.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7e1203.png
omega: omega
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes
evaluate: -iea0


[AS7's Example 12.11 (wye-delta with line impedances)]

ea1,na1,0,100
eb1,nb1,0,(100∠-120°)
ec1,nc1,0,(100∠120°)
raa,na1,na2,1
rbb,nb1,nb2,1
rcc,nc1,nc2,1
rac,na2,nc2,100+24*pi*j
rcb,nc2,nb2,100+24*pi*j
rba,nb2,na2,100+24*pi*j

analysis: ac
note: Find the line current IaA (iraa), the phase voltage VAB (the Evaluate line, vna2-vnb2) and the phase current IAC (irac). The load's three nodes are separate from the source's because of the line resistors.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7e1211.png
omega: omega
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes
evaluate: vna2-vnb2


[AS7's Example 12.4 (balanced delta-delta)]

e0a,0,ag,(330∠120°)
eb0,bg,0,(330∠-120°)
sat,ag,ad
sbt,bg,bd
sct,0,cd
rab,ad,bd,20-15j
rbc,bd,cd,20-15j
rca,cd,ad,20-15j

analysis: ac
note: Find the load's phase currents and the line currents — the currents through the three shorts that act as the lines. A triangle of three voltage sources cannot be solved -- the third adds an unknown but no information -- so the source opposite the ground node is left out. Everything outside the delta is right; the currents inside the generator are not.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7e1204.png
omega: omega
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes


