[AS7's Example 12.12 (unbalanced delta-delta)]

e0a,0,ag,(208∠130°)
eb0,bg,0,(208∠-110°)
rla,ag,ad,2+5j
rlb,bg,bd,2+5j
rlc,0,cd,2+5j
rab,ad,bd,50
rbc,bd,cd,30j
rca,cd,ad,-40j

analysis: ac
note: Find the generator current Iab, the line current IbB (irlb) and the phase current IBC (irbc). The generator current Iab cannot be had this way: it is a current inside the delta, and the two-source trick gives up exactly that. aa(-(ie0a+ieb0)/3) happens to land on the book's figure — a guess that was checked, not a method.
image: https://learn.symbulator.com/assets/circuit/as7e1212.png
omega: omega
rounding: 4
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: yes


